<usx version="3.0"><chapter number="4" style="c" sid=" 4" /><para style="cl">Chapter Four</para><para style="cd">This chapter description (cd) follows the chapter label (cl). Chapter 4 exercises standard USFM that chapters 1 through 3 do not use, plus shapes that pin known converter bugs. Chapter 5 holds deliberately damaged USFM.</para><para style="s1">A section heading before verse 1</para><para style="r">(2 Sam 4.1-12)</para><para style="b" /><para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="" />A cross reference<note caller="+" style="x"><char style="xo" closed="false">4.1: </char><char style="xt" closed="false">1 Sam 31.4; 2 Sam 1.1</char></note> sits mid-verse. This verse ends with a footnote butted against the next verse marker with no space between them.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">4.1 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">A footnote that ends right before the next verse marker.</char></note> <verse eid="" /><verse number="2-3" style="v" pubnumber="2-3a" sid="" /> Verse bridge 2-3 carrying a published verse number (vp). <verse eid="" /><verse number="4a" style="v" sid="" />Verse segment 4a. <verse eid="" /><verse number="4b" style="v" sid="" />Verse segment 4b. <verse eid="" /><verse number="5" style="v" sid="" />An endnote<note caller="+" style="fe"><char style="fr" closed="false">4.5 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">Endnote text.</char></note> then a footnote with no caller<note caller="-" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">4.5 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">The minus caller means no caller is shown.</char></note> then one with a custom caller<note caller="a" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">4.5 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">Custom caller a.</char></note> end. <verse eid="" /><verse number="6" style="v" sid="" />Non-breaking spaces: a character span whose whole content is a NBSP <char style="nd"> </char>, one with a leading NBSP <char style="nd"> lead</char>, one with a trailing NBSP <char style="nd">trail </char>, a NBSP before punctuation mot : and one inside a number 1 000.</para><para style="p" vid=""> </para><para style="p" vid="">The paragraph above has a lone NBSP as its only content. This paragraph ends with a space before an unknown marker </para><para style="zunk" status="unknown" vid="">Unknown marker content.</para><para style="p" vid="">Authored references: a closed <verse eid="" /></para><para style="ref" status="unknown">1 Sam 1.1|1SA 1:1<unmatched marker="ref*" /> and an unclosed </para><para style="ref" status="unknown">1 Sam 2.1|1SA 2:1 that runs to the end of the paragraph.</para><chapter eid=" 4" /></usx>